# Snapmaker patterns

## Connectivity

| Channel | Port | Use for |
|---------|------|---------|
| HTTP API v1 | `8080` | Connect (token), status poll, (later) control endpoints |

Base URL: `http://<host>:8080/api/v1`

### Auth flow

1. `POST /connect` without token → machine returns `{ token, series, headType, … }` and shows confirm dialog on touchscreen
2. Until confirmed, status may return `204 No Content` — keep polling status so the dialog stays alive
3. After confirm, `POST /connect` with `token=<token>` (form-urlencoded) reuses the token
4. Persist token (e.g. adapter state or local file under `this.adapterDir` / compact data); do not put token in `native` admin config
5. On `401` / denied: clear token and restart connect flow

### Status poll

`GET /status?token=<token>` (optional cache-buster timestamp as Luban does)

Important JSON fields (names may vary slightly by firmware — normalize in one place):

| API field | State | Notes |
|-----------|-------|-------|
| `status` | `status` | `IDLE` / `RUNNING` / `PAUSED` / … |
| `fileName` | `currentJob.fileName` | Current / last job |
| `progress` | `currentJob.progress` | Often `0..1` → expose as `0..100` % |
| `elapsedTime` | `currentJob.elapsedTime` | Seconds |
| `remainingTime` | `currentJob.remainingTime` | Seconds |
| `toolHead` / `headType` | `info.toolHead`, `laser.modulePower` | e.g. `10W LASER` → label + watts |
| `x` / `y` / `z` | `info.x` / `y` / `z` | mm, rounded to 0.001 |
| `homed` | `info.homed` | boolean |
| `isEnclosureDoorOpen` | `enclosure.doorOpen` | boolean |
| `currentLine` / `totalLines` | `currentJob.currentLine` / `totalLines` | G-code progress |

## Curated state tree (do not dump entire status JSON)

```
snapmaker.0.
  info.connection
  info.series, toolHead
  info.x, y, z, homed
  status
  currentJob.fileName
  currentJob.progress            (%)
  currentJob.elapsedTime         (s)
  currentJob.remainingTime       (s)
  currentJob.finishAt            (local YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM)
  currentJob.currentLine, totalLines
  enclosure.doorOpen
```

## Source of truth for behavior

Implement in `lib/snapmakerApi.js` (HTTP helpers) + thin orchestration in `main.js`.
Reference community implementations for field names if needed (Home Assistant Snapmaker integrations, Luban), but keep inventwo state naming (`currentJob.*`).
